{"name":"Rouge","hex":"#ab1239","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rouge","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A neighbourhood of Toronto, Ontario, Canada.","A surname from French."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rouge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rouge (cosmetics)","blocks":[{"text":"Rouge, also called blush or blusher, is a cosmetic for coloring the cheeks in a variety of shades, or the lips red. It is applied as a powder, cream or liquid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Make-up_box_MAN_Paestum_T.4-1990.jpg/330px-Make-up_box_MAN_Paestum_T.4-1990.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rouge_(cosmetics)"},{"title":"Iron(III) oxide","blocks":[{"text":"Iron(III) oxide or ferric oxide is the inorganic compound with the formula Fe2O3. It occurs in nature as the mineral hematite, which serves as the primary source of iron for the steel industry. It is also known as red iron oxide, especially when used in pigments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Haematite-unit-cell-3D-balls.png/330px-Haematite-unit-cell-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron(III)_oxide"},{"title":"Rouge (group)","blocks":[{"text":"Rouge was a Brazilian pop girl group formed in 2002, consisting of Aline Wirley, Fantine Thó, Karin Hils, Li Martins and Lu Andrade. The members of the group were selected during the first season of the Brazilian adaptation of the reality talent show Popstars and mentored by producer Rick Bonadio."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Rouge_Vila_Velha_2018.jpg/330px-Rouge_Vila_Velha_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rouge_(group)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c